[S1-F1] high — comma-OR `--key` bypasses the amended statusless-only refusal. The census runs before Surface applies `key_or`, so an unrelated status-bearing row changes exit 2 into a plausible-empty exit 0. [dispatch.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/apps/loops/src/loops/cli/dispatch.py:134)

```text
$ loops read <statusv> --key design/a --status open --plain
exit=2
stdout: (empty)
stderr: read --status: kind 'decision' has no status field ...

$ loops read <statusv> --key design/a,missing --status open --plain
exit=0
stdout: No data yet.
stderr: note: kind 'decision' has no status field — --status cannot match it
```

Both select the same statusless `decision/design/a`; only the comma spelling fetches the unrelated status-bearing thread before filtering.

[S1-F2] high — static custom-lens reads accept `--status`, ignore it, render unfiltered rows, and exit 0. This violates both payload-equality filtering and the statusless-only exit-2 amendment. [dispatch.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/apps/loops/src/loops/cli/dispatch.py:423)

